From tober@bbnplanet.com  Mon Dec 30 18:20:26 1996
From: Ben Tober <tober@bbnplanet.com>
To: port-alpha@NetBSD.ORG
Date: Mon, 30 Dec 1996 18:20:26 +0000
Subject: Upgrading AXPpci33 firmware

I'm having a strange problem trying to upgrade the firmware on a
very old AXPpci33s system.  I have read the directions and downloaded the
disk images from gatekeeper in /pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/interim/multia and
set the jumper for a failsafe boot (upgrading from the ARC console is not
an option here since the system is too old to have had the ARC console).
On power-on, the system reads the failsafe boot floppy, displays a one-line
SRM Console banner, then hangs.  Any ideas?  Have there been multiple
versions of PALcode for the AXPpci33?  Could mine be too old to accomodate
the current firmware?
-ben

From matt@lkg.dec.com  Mon Dec 30 19:52:15 1996
From: Matt Thomas <matt@lkg.dec.com>
To: tober@bbnplanet.com
Date: Mon, 30 Dec 1996 19:52:15 +0000
Subject: Re: Upgrading AXPpci33 firmware

The axppci33 is not the same thing as a multia.  putting in multia
firmware is a *bad* thing.

You want the firware from:

ftp://gatekeeper.dec.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/v3.8/decaxppci33/decaxppci33_v1
_6.sys (or .exe).


